          <p>
            Ensure Max Protein 3-in-1 costs about $2.05 to $2.45 per 25 g of protein, and Ensure Original powder costs about $4.30 to $5.40, so the newer tub is less than half the price per gram of protein. We use cost per 25 g because tub prices hide how much protein you are actually buying, and these two products differ by more than three times in protein per serving.
          </p>

          <p>
            The arithmetic for the 3-in-1: a tub makes 15 servings of 30 g, so 450 g of protein, or 18 portions of 25 g. Walmart listed the 28 oz chocolate tub at $36.98 in autumn 2026, which is $2.05 per 25 g. The Abbott Store charged $87.98 for a two-tub pack in November 2026, or $43.99 a tub, which is $2.44 per 25 g. Those prices also buy you 5 g of creatine a day, which on its own costs roughly 10 to 30 cents a serving in a plain tub, so the protein part is closer to $1.90 to $2.30.
          </p>

